2.explanation:
In Dropdown.js, each dropdown option is rendered with both inner text and a "title" prop: 

    <ListBox.MenuItem
      ...
      title={itemToString(item)}
      {...itemProps}
    >
      {itemToString(item)}
    </ListBox.MenuItem>

Because ListBoxMenuItem (in ListBoxMenuItem.js) spreads that title prop onto the DOM node, VoiceOver picks up both the visible text and the title attribute and reads them separately. Removing or changing the title attribute (for example using aria-label or omitting title entirely) will prevent the duplicate announcement.
